    <briefdescription>
<para><computeroutput><ref refid="class_word" kindref="compound">Word</ref></computeroutput> plus its ecart degree and heft degree <mdash/> the value type <computeroutput><ref refid="class_word_with_data_table" kindref="compound">WordWithDataTable</ref></computeroutput> stores. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><computeroutput><ref refid="class_word_with_data_afed4b70763866f32b942f9a3109060b4_1afed4b70763866f32b942f9a3109060b4" kindref="member">mEcartDegree</ref></computeroutput> records the power of an invisible homogenising variable so divisibility checks in <computeroutput><ref refid="class_word_with_data_table_a18978a08954516e567a7f34d57272997_1a18978a08954516e567a7f34d57272997" kindref="member">WordWithDataTable::subword</ref></computeroutput> can refuse matches whose ecart is wrong; <computeroutput><ref refid="class_word_with_data_a8b0e8157ba9ffc0e29341eb7640b29ff_1a8b0e8157ba9ffc0e29341eb7640b29ff" kindref="member">mHeftDegree</ref></computeroutput> is the original heft degree the word entered with, kept for stable sorting. The underlying word is held by composition (<computeroutput><ref refid="class_word_with_data_aea75eed6a463c482bfb13644e0c1b670_1aea75eed6a463c482bfb13644e0c1b670" kindref="member">mWord</ref></computeroutput>) rather than inheritance. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
